[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2753955811","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104641#issuecomment-2753955811","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104641","id":2753955811,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kJgfj","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-26T10:35:50Z","updated_at":"2025-03-26T10:35:50Z","body":"See https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/assets_pipeline/import_process.html\n\nPNGs are imported resources, only result of import process (e.g, `.godot/imported/example.png-{hash}.ctex`) is exported, and original file is not.\n\nYou can still load it using original name, but `DirAccess` won't see it since file is not these, use [ResourceLoader.list_directory](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_resourceloader.html#class-resourceloader-method-list-directory) to list imported resources instead.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2753955811/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2754068256","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104641#issuecomment-2754068256","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104641","id":2754068256,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kJ78g","user":{"login":"miruji","id":147953988,"node_id":"U_kgDOCNGZRA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/147953988?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji","html_url":"https://github.com/miruji","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-26T11:21:01Z","updated_at":"2025-03-26T11:21:01Z","body":"ResourceLoader.list_directory(path) works and can see .png files.\n\nDoes this mean that the .png.import in the exported version only references the .ctex? Then why do the .png files used in scenes remain as .png during export? Does this work the same way for all file types or only for images?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2754068256/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2754093775","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104641#issuecomment-2754093775","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104641","id":2754093775,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kKCLP","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-26T11:31:40Z","updated_at":"2025-03-26T11:31:40Z","body":"> Does this mean that the .png.import in the exported version only references the .ctex?\n\nIt is referencing both source and imported files, like:\n```\n[remap]\nuid=\"uid://cscq80dsfslik\"\npath=\"res://.godot/imported/icon.svg-218a8f2b3041327d8a5756f3a245f83b.ctex\" <------ processed file\n\n[deps]\nsource_file=\"res://icon.svg\" <------ source file\n```\n\n> Then why do the .png files used in scenes remain as .png during export?\n\nIt should not. But you can reference any of these files by its original name in the scene.\n\n> Does this work the same way for all file types or only for images?\n\nFor all types that are imported (if you see something in the `Import` tab when file is selected in the editor file system it is imported), `.ctex` is image specific. Similar thing is done for scene/resources/scripts, these are converted to binary format/compiled `.tscn` → `.scn` / `.gd` → `.gdc` and have `.remap` file added during export instead of `.import`.\n\nYou can export project content as ZIP (select `Export PCK/ZIP` in the export dialog and change file extension top `.zip`) to check what's actually exported for your project.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2754093775/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":1,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2754144006","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104641#issuecomment-2754144006","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104641","id":2754144006,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kKOcG","user":{"login":"miruji","id":147953988,"node_id":"U_kgDOCNGZRA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/147953988?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji","html_url":"https://github.com/miruji","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-26T11:53:27Z","updated_at":"2025-03-26T11:53:27Z","body":"I see, thank you, this is very important information!\n\nI checked and I can see everything is in imported, which means that load() only works with resources that are known to the compiler in advance? In any case, you can't initially access them with DirAccess and load() since they work with surface-level resources?\n\nAnd yet, this was simply not in the documentation for these functions, although I checked them before creating the issue. It only says that one is for simple cases and the other is for more complex ones, but it doesn't describe this.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2754144006/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2754166538","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104641#issuecomment-2754166538","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104641","id":2754166538,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kKT8K","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-26T12:00:19Z","updated_at":"2025-03-26T12:00:19Z","body":"> which means that load() only works with resources that are known to the compiler in advance?\n\nYou can load external files, but instead of `load` a specific class for a file type should be used. E.g, [Image.load](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_image.html#class-image-method-load) and [ImageTexture.create_from_image](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_imagetexture.html#class-imagetexture-method-create-from-image) in case of textures.\n\n> And yet, this was simply not in the documentation for these functions\n\nDirAcces have a note [about it](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_diraccess.html#description) in the description, but it probably should be mentioned in the `load` docs as well.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2754166538/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]